       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 10 mg daily. Higher doses raise the risk of significant hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and they usually add little blood-pressure benefit.\n\nHere are some ways to proceed:\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO daily**, titrated up to 10 mg. This is the usual starting dose.\n3. **A second agent** if 10 mg isn't enough, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic. Combining agents is generally better than going above the maximum.\n\nIf you meant 20 mg, or the 20 mg is intentional, tell me and I can enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Or tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
